    "overview": {
      "text": "Hoover Dam is a concrete arch-gravity dam in Black Canyon of the Colorado River, on the Nevada–Arizona border southeast of Las Vegas. Built as part of the federal Boulder Canyon Project, it was designed to help control floods, store water for farms and cities, and generate hydroelectric power. Construction began in 1931; the dam began impounding water in Lake Mead on February 1, 1935, and its last concrete was placed that May. The project reshaped the arid Southwest and became a landmark of large-scale engineering. First known as Boulder Dam, it was officially named Hoover Dam in 1947.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://www.nps.gov/articles/nevada-and-arizona-hoover-dam.htm",
        "https://www.usbr.gov/history/hoover.html",
        "https://www.usbr.gov/lc/hooverdam/history/articles/chrono.html"
      ]
    },
    "key_facts": [
      {
        "text": "The dam stands in Black Canyon, where the Colorado River forms the Nevada–Arizona border.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.usbr.gov/history/hoover.html"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "It is an arch-gravity dam, 726 feet above the riverbed; its concrete base is 660 feet thick.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.nps.gov/articles/nevada-and-arizona-hoover-dam.htm"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The dam began holding back water to form Lake Mead on February 1, 1935. Its last concrete was placed May 29, 1935; President Franklin D. Roosevelt dedicated it that September.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.usbr.gov/lc/hooverdam/history/articles/chrono.html"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Its planned roles included flood control, water storage for farms and cities, and hydroelectric power generation.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.nps.gov/articles/nevada-and-arizona-hoover-dam.htm"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Congress officially designated it Hoover Dam in 1947, after it had also been called Boulder Dam.",
        "source_urls": [
          "https://www.usbr.gov/lc/hooverdam/history/articles/chrono.html",
          "https://www.nps.gov/articles/nevada-and-arizona-hoover-dam.htm"
        ]
      }
